Subtitle renderer (libass-sn.so.0)
----------------------------------
libass-sn.so.0 is the StremioNative facade (native/ass.c, native/ass_fonts.c, GPL-3.0-or-later)
statically linked with this pinned stack, built by ci/build-libass.py from the checksum-pinned
upstream archives recorded in ci/dependencies.json:

  libass       0.17.5   ISC                                   licenses/libass-ISC.txt
  FreeType     2.15.0   FreeType License; MIT and Zlib parts  licenses/FreeType.txt, licenses/Zlib.txt
  FriBidi      1.0.17   LGPL-2.1-or-later                     licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt
  HarfBuzz     14.6.0   Old MIT                               licenses/HarfBuzz-Old-MIT.txt
  libunibreak  8.0      Zlib                                  licenses/libunibreak-Zlib.txt

Portions of this software are copyright (C) 2026 The FreeType Project (https://freetype.org).
All rights reserved. Its built-in gzip reader contains zlib 1.3.1, Copyright (C) 1995-2024
Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler. FriBidi is Copyright (C) 1999, 2000, 2017-2019 Dov Grobgeld;
2001, 2002, 2004, 2005 Behdad Esfahbod; 2004 Sharif FarsiWeb, Inc.; and other contributors.
libunibreak is Copyright (C) Wu Yongwei, Tom Hacohen, Petr Filipsky and Andreas Roever. The libass
and HarfBuzz copyright notices are retained in their licence files.

libass carries one local patch, ci/patches/libass-0001-grow-font-faces.patch (ISC, like libass):
it replaces the fixed table of ten font faces per font with arrays that grow on demand, so a track
that uses many scripts is not cut off at the tenth face. Every other archive is unmodified. The
stack is built without fontconfig or any system font provider; the fonts it draws with ship in the
package (appfont*.ttf, fonts/subs/). You may rebuild the library, including FriBidi, from the
matching source release and replace libass-sn.so.0 in the app directory; the application loads it
by name from there and checks the facade ABI. No library in this stack comes from the television.

Dolby Vision Profile 7 to 8.1 conversion
----------------------------------------
crates/media/src/dovi.rs ports the RPU conversion of dovi_tool's `dolby_vision` crate 3.4.0
(ConversionMode::To81, `dovi_tool convert --mode 2`; https://github.com/quietvoid/dovi_tool,
commit 614c816), Copyright (c) 2026 quietvoid, MIT licence: licenses/dovi_tool-MIT.txt. The RPU
test fixtures in tests/fixtures/dovi/ are dovi_tool's own test assets and its library's output for
them, under the same licence.
